<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clonfert</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clonfert is a village in east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a>, Ireland, where St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brendan-the-navigator">Brendan the Navigator</a> founded a monastery around 557. The monastery became a major centre of learning and the seat of a medieval bishopric. Its 12th-century cathedral has a celebrated Hiberno-Romanesque doorway, one of the finest in Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clonfert.jpg" alt="Clonfert" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas F. Borchert · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clonfert_Cathedral_Portal_Left_Jamb_Interlace_Pattern_2009_09_17.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
